<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta http-equiv="X-UA-Compatible" content="IE=edge">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">

  {%- comment -%} Cobalt derives a title from the filename when front matter has none, so the
    homepage rendered as "Index" everywhere and no other page named the site. {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign page_title = page.title | default: site.title -%}
  <title>{% if page_title == site.title %}{{ site.title | escape }} &mdash; the state of machine learning in Rust{% else %}{{ page_title | escape }} &mdash; {{ site.title | escape }}{% endif %}</title>
  {%- comment -%}
    An excerpt carries the markdown source's line wraps, and `strip_newlines` joins them with no
    separator -- /gpu/ shipped "Metal,DirectX 12" -- so the split and join below is that operation
    with a space. Truncating before the escape keeps the 160 counting characters rather than the
    middle of an entity. The site-wide fallback is not truncated: it was written to be a
    description, and cutting it left every prose page ending mid-clause.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- capture newline %}
{% endcapture -%}
  {%- if page.excerpt -%}
    {%- assign meta_description = page.excerpt | strip_html | split: newline | join: " " | strip | truncate: 160 -%}
  {%- else -%}
    {%- assign meta_description = site.description | split: newline | join: " " | strip -%}
  {%- endif %}
  <meta name="description" content="{{ meta_description | escape }}">

  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/main.css">

  <link rel="canonical" href="{{ page.permalink | replace:'index.html','' | prepend: '/' | prepend: site.base_url | escape }}">

  <link rel="apple-touch-icon" sizes="180x180" href="/images/apple-touch-icon.png">
  <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="/images/favicon-32x32.png" sizes="32x32">
  <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="/images/favicon-16x16.png" sizes="16x16">
  <link rel="manifest" href="/manifest.json">
  <link rel="mask-icon" href="/images/safari-pinned-tab.svg" color="#b7410e">
  <meta name="theme-color" content="#b7410e">
</head>
